.TH PDP1 1 "November 2026" "pidp1-mods" "PiDP-1 Commands"
.SH NAME
pdp1 \- attach to the running PDP-1 simulator, or start a front-end program beside it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY pdp1
.YS
.SY pdp1
.IR option
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdp1
is the front door to the PDP-1 emulator of the
.BR pidp1-mods (7)
package.
With no arguments it attaches to the
.BR screen (1)
session of the simulator started by
.BR pdp1control (1);
detach again with Ctrl-A d.
With one argument it starts a front-end program next to the running
simulator, without disturbing it:
.TP
.B con
the noisy Teletype model 33, connected to the emulator's Teletype port.
The Teletype is the PiDP-10 project's
.BR sty ;
if it is not at
.IR /opt/pidp10/bin/sty ,
point
.B PIDP10_STY
at it, or use
.B pdp1 soroban
instead.
.TP
.B soroban
a terminal window on the Soroban typewriter port.
.TP
.B ptr
choose a paper tape in a dialog and mount it on the reader.
.TP
.B ptp
save the paper tape punch output to a file.
.TP
.B tape
the tape reader and punch window (tapevis).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PIDP1_ENV
Where to find the locations file
.IR pidp1-env.sh ;
by default the one beside this script.
.TP
.B PIDP10_STY
Path of the PiDP-10 noisy Teletype used by the
.B con
command.
.PP
All the location variables
.IR pidp1-env.sh (PIDP1_DATADIR,
PIDP1_STATEDIR, PIDP1_SYSCONFDIR, PIDP1_BINDIR, PIDP1_LIBEXECDIR) may be
set to point the whole tool set at a build tree or a test root.
.SH FILES
.TP
/usr/share/pidp1-mods
read-only program data
.TP
/var/lib/pidp1-mods
drum image, punch output, the tape library the boot configurations mount
.TP
/etc/pidp1-mods
site configuration
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 when the requested program was started (or the screen session attached);
non-zero when the simulator is not running or the front end could not start.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pdp1control (1),
.BR pdp1central (1),
.BR screen (1)
